## Nuke build outputs (dotnet test results / ReportGenerator output; the original
## workflow wrote these under CI-only paths and never gitignored them - now that
## `nuke Test`/`nuke Coverage` are easy to run locally too, ignore them for real)
TestResults/
coverage/
## Nuke scratch dir (build.schema.json and parameters.json ARE tracked)
.nuke/temp/

## Knowledge-graph output (/graphify). Ignore the derived and machine-local parts,
## but TRACK cache/semantic + manifest.json so the LLM extraction is shared across
## dev machines instead of being paid for again on each one. The semantic cache is
## the only part that costs tokens; AST extraction and graph.json/graph.html are
## deterministic and regenerate in seconds from the tracked cache.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cache/*
!graphify-out/cache/semantic/
!graphify-out/manifest.json
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md

